# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev-server asset stores (no PUBLIC_ prefix — these never reach the browser)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the Astro dev server READS the heavy assets from. The dev middleware serves
# /heroes, /borders and /tiles straight off these directories; the static build never
# reads them.
#
# Required for `astro dev`: copy this file to .env and set each to your local path.
# There is no fallback — an unset var fails the dev server with a clear message.
# (`astro build` does not need them.)
HERO_STORE=/path/to/maps/blender/renders/variants
BORDERS_STORE=/path/to/maps/data/work/borders
# PMTILES_STORE holds the packaged archive (planet.pmtiles) — the /tiles route opens it
# and answers z/x/y out of it; it is the sole relief tile source.
PMTILES_STORE=/path/to/maps/data/work/planet_tiles
# TERRAIN_PMTILES_STORE holds the packaged elevation archive (terrain.pmtiles), which the same
# /tiles route answers under the /tiles/terrain/ prefix. Separate from PMTILES_STORE because the
# two are products of two different pipeline outputs; in production they are two object keys in
# one R2 bucket. Only needed if you run the globe at the `full` tier or with ?terrain=N.
TERRAIN_PMTILES_STORE=/path/to/maps/data/work/planet_terrain

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deploy preflight (no PUBLIC_ prefix — never reaches the browser)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The R2 S3 endpoint, used by scripts/check_deploy_sync.ts to confirm R2 holds every hero
# the manifest is about to advertise. Set only if you deploy; `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build`
# ignore it. It lives here rather than in the repo because the account ID is part of the URL.
# Credentials come from the `r2` profile in ~/.aws/credentials, not from this file.
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset base URLs (PUBLIC_ prefix — inlined into the pages and the client bundle)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the built site ADDRESSES those same assets. Unset means same-origin, which is what
# the dev server and the nginx prod-sim serve — so LEAVE THESE UNSET. They are listed here
# to document that they exist, not to be filled in.
#
# The production values are NOT configured here. They live in `build:deploy` in
# package.json, because that is the only place that can guarantee the deploy and its
# hostnames ship together: `.env.production` is gitignored (root `.env.*`, which exists to
# keep OPENTOPOGRAPHY_API_KEY out of git), so a committed one would need a hole in that
# guard, and an uncommitted one is hidden state a fresh checkout cannot reproduce.
#
# Setting them here instead breaks local work quietly: `astro dev` would serve the site
# shell locally while pulling tiles and heroes from production, so the dev middleware and
# the local archive are never exercised and a broken one looks fine.
#
# See src/lib/assetBase.ts for the resolution rule; a missing trailing slash is added.
#
# PUBLIC_HERO_BASE=https://assets.example.com/heroes/
# PUBLIC_BORDERS_BASE=https://assets.example.com/borders/
# PUBLIC_TILE_BASE=https://tiles.example.com/
